# Imdb API

> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.

## Documentation Index
- `SKILL.md` (this file)
- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)
- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)
- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)

## Authentication
Unknown (may need login) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Data Read (26)
- `GET /{id}` — Get movie/show details by ID.
- `GET /{id}/{id}` — Get data using two IDs.
- `GET /ad/u` — Get ad-related user data.
- `GET /AdServer/js/user_sync.html` — Get user synchronization script.
- `GET /adx/user/sync` — Synchronize user data with ad exchange.
- `GET /api/cookie` — Retrieve a cookie value.
- `GET /api/v1/{v1Id}` — Retrieve data for a specific IMDb entity (v1Id).
- `GET /api/v1/dsync/amazon` — Synchronize data with Amazon's IMDb data.
- `GET /api/v1/p/{pId}` — Retrieve data for a specific IMDb person (pId).
- `GET /api/v1/u/matches/{matcheId}` — Retrieve match data for a user (matcheId).
- `GET /bh/rtset` — Get real-time set data.
- `GET /dis/usersync.aspx` — Synchronize user data.
- `GET /display/{displayId}/{displayId}` — Get data using two display IDs.
- `GET /getuid/id5` — Get a user ID.
- `GET /jwumXNuB/v1/` — Get version 1 data.
- `GET /t/v2` — Get version 2 data.
- `GET /t/v2/sync` — Synchronize version 2 data.
- `GET /user-sync/{user-syncId}` — Get user sync data by ID.
- `GET /userPixel/syncr` — Synchronize user pixel data.
- `GET /usersync/{usersyncId}` — Get user sync data by ID.
- `GET /usersync/audigent/0` — Synchronize user data with Audigent.
- `GET /usersync2/rubicon` — Synchronize user data with Rubicon.
- `GET /usync/{usyncId}` — Get user sync data by ID.
- `GET /v1/{v1Id}` — Get version 1 data by ID.
- `GET /v1/ad-events/loaded/{loadedId}` — Track when an advertisement has loaded.
- `GET /v1/api/sync/{syncId}` — Synchronize data using a specific sync ID.

### Data Write (4)
- `POST /{id}` — Write or update data for a specific entity (id).
- `POST /6/map` — Post data to a map endpoint.
- `POST /api/_ajax/metrics/ops/` — Submit operational metrics to IMDb.
- `POST /data/cors` — Post data for Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS).

### Media (1)
- `GET /api/user/image/{imageHash}` — Download a user profile image by its hash.

### Realtime (1)
- `POST /1/events/{eventId}` — Report a real-time event to IMDb (eventId).

### Config (1)
- `GET /cdn/prod/config` — Get configuration settings for the IMDb website.

## Quick Start

Here are some quick start examples to get you going with the IMDb API:

```typescript
// Get movie details by ID (e.g., tt0111161 for The Shawshank Redemption)
